{"title":"Career roadmap · Supply Chain Analyst","role":"Supply Chain Analyst","summary":"A Supply Chain Analyst analyses procurement, inventory, transportation, warehousing, demand, suppliers and operational performance to improve the flow of products and information through a supply chain.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"B.Com","Course":"Logistics & Supply Chain","Timeline assumption":"3- or 4-year B.Com pathway depending on the university. If a four-year honours/research structure is followed, use the additional year for advanced supply-chain analytics, internships and a research/capstone project."},"about":[{"label":"Primary skills","text":"Supply-chain management, Excel, SQL, Power BI, statistics, inventory analysis, forecasting"},{"label":"Additional skills","text":"ERP, Python, optimisation, demand planning, procurement analytics, AI"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Supply Chain Intern, Logistics Analyst Intern, Procurement Intern, Operations Intern"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Supply Chain Analyst, Logistics Analyst, Demand Planning Analyst, Procurement Analyst"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Supply Chain Analyst, Supply Chain Planner, S&OP Analyst, Supply Chain Consultant"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Supply Chain Analytics Lead, Planning Manager, Supply Chain Manager, Operations Manager"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Com Logistics & Supply Chain graduate, this is a very strong and direct career alignment. The student should combine supply-chain knowledge with Excel, SQL, Power BI, statistics, ERP systems, forecasting and optimisation."},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Logistics & Supply Chain","Supply Chain/Operations Internship","Supply Chain Analyst / Logistics Analyst","Senior Supply Ch